  "summary_en": "Japan's Digital Agency issues trademark and brand guidelines for \"Government AI Genai\", its generative AI environment for ministries, partly open-sourced. It separates code licensing from brand elements and sets display rules by user type, modification level and provision method. It also prescribes standard disclaimers and a contact and enforcement process.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Copyright/code licence (OSS) is separated from permission to use the name and official logo.",
   "Descriptive references to the relationship need no prior permission.",
   "Derivatives must have their own names and must not use the official name or logo.",
   "Users are classed into five categories, with display permissions set by modification degree and provision method.",
   "Mandatory notices: derivative, embedding and anti-misidentification statements; Digital Agency handles inquiries and misuse reports."
  ],
